    <!-- 2026-11-22 polish: triggers off by default (ADR-005), contextual help (UX-002) -->
    <string name="battery_triggers_off_title">No automatic trigger is on</string>
    <string name="battery_triggers_off_body">Nothing starts on its own. A profile becomes active only when you start it or turn on one of its triggers.</string>
    <string name="battery_battery_triggers_title">Battery triggers</string>
    <string name="battery_monitor_resume_title">Resume after restart</string>
    <string name="battery_retention_more_title">What gets deleted</string>
    <string name="battery_retention_more_summary">Notes and baseline go with the history</string>
    <string name="battery_help_pause_triggers">What it does: every automatic trigger is ignored until you turn this off. Profiles you started by hand stay active; trigger settings stay saved.\n\nRisk: none. Battery, schedule and screen-off triggers will not react while paused.\n\nUndo: turn the switch off.</string>
    <string name="battery_help_monitor">What it does: the live monitor runs as a foreground service, so Android shows an ongoing notification while it is on. It listens to battery and screen events and reads current at most every 5 minutes. Only session summaries are saved, on this device.\n\nCost: monitoring itself uses a little battery. Able does not claim savings from it.\n\nUndo: tap Stop here or in the notification.</string>
    <string name="battery_help_resume">What it does: if the monitor was running when the phone restarts, Able starts it again after boot so tracking continues. If you stopped it, it stays off.\n\nRisk: the ongoing notification reappears after a restart.\n\nUndo: stop the monitor; it will not resume.</string>
    <string name="battery_help_reset_rules">What it does: these rules set the live statistics back to zero on an event (charger connected, device restart, battery level). Saved sessions are not deleted.\n\nRisk: you lose the current since-reset totals.\n\nUndo: turn the rule off. A reset that already happened cannot be reversed.</string>
    <string name="battery_help_delete_history">What it does: permanently removes saved sessions, their notes and the personal baseline, and resets the live statistics. Profiles and app rules are kept.\n\nRisk: this cannot be undone and Able keeps no copy. The baseline needs several new nights to rebuild.\n\nUndo: not possible. You will be asked to confirm first.</string>
    <string name="battery_help_advanced">What it does: with Shizuku, Able runs a read-only command that reads battery files exposed by the kernel (capacity, cycles, dates). Nothing is written or changed.\n\nRisk: Shizuku gives apps elevated access; authorize only apps you trust. Many devices hide these fields or report approximate values.\n\nUndo: nothing to undo. You can revoke Able in Shizuku at any time.</string>
